    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it passes along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` response field \u2014 a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode`.\n\nChanges, each kept to its proper layer:\n\n1. **`util/Luhn.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, reusable, single-responsibility utility. `Luhn.checkDigit(String)` computes the Luhn check digit (0\u20139) over the digit characters of any string, ignoring non-digits (so it works directly on the formatted `PAR-FRA-0007` code). It mirrors the standard algorithm the acceptance test uses.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` alongside the other derived fields, plus a thin `checkDigit(Owner)` default method that delegates to `Luhn.checkDigit(...)` and returns `null` when `customerCode` is absent (consistent with how `membershipNumber` handles missing sources). No algorithm logic leaked into the mapper.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `checkDigit` integer property (int32) to the owner schema, next to `customerCode`, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\nThe Luhn computation lives in `util` (reusable/testable), the mapper only wires it, and the DTO contract is declared in the spec \u2014 no catch-all class grew as a result.",
